{
  "name": "Period phrase \u2014 antecedent (HC) + consequent (PAC), 4-voice",
  "description": "Demonstrates r-cadence and r-repetition together on a classical period, PLUS the chord-tone-membership and no-parallel-fifths/octaves rules every real 4-part config needs alongside them — r-cadence and r-repetition only constrain the specific voices/positions they're asked to, so without these accompanying rules the other voices are free to produce arbitrary, musically incoherent results. Antecedent (0-7) ends in a half cadence (ii-V); consequent (8-15) echoes the antecedent's soprano contour (soft) and ends in a full authentic cadence (hard: root position, soprano on tonic). Known simplification: chord-tone rules check each voice individually, not collective chord coverage, so e.g. the final V7 may omit its 3rd/7th in favor of doubled root/5th.",
  "solution_length": 16,
  "num_voices": 4,
  "search_options": {
    "engine": "dfs",
    "enable_metric_engine": 0,
    "random_seed": 0,
    "timeout_ms": 20000,
    "branching": "first_fail",
    "value_order": "min"
  },
  "export_json": false,
  "export_txt": true,
  "export_xml": true,
